   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region; the stereocentres were assigned from the wedges and hashes by working out each centre's CIP priorities by hand, and I did not run it through a toolkit.\n\n**Regions of the molecule**\n- **Piperazic acid ring:** A six-membered hexahydropyridazine. Its C3 carries the ester carbonyl on a hashed bond and is labelled (S). The adjacent NH is free, and the other ring nitrogen is acylated by the amino acid carbonyl.\n- **Macrocyclic linker:** The ester oxygen connects through OCH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2 to C3 of the indole.\n- **Indole:**\n  - C2 carries a pyridin-3-yl group, which has a (S)-1-methoxyethyl group on the carbon next to the ring nitrogen.\n  - N1 carries an ethyl group.\n  - C5 is bonded to C4 of the thiazole.\n- **Thiazole:** C2 carries a CH2 that leads to the (S) \u03b1-carbon of the amino acid. That \u03b1-carbon bears the NH of the urea and the acyl carbonyl attached to the piperazic nitrogen.\n- **Urea side chain:** NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013N(CH3)\u2013CH2\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013OCH3, with the methoxy-bearing carbon labelled (S).\n\n**Stereodescriptors in the SMILES:** `[C@@H]1` for the piperazic carbon, `[C@H]` for the amino acid \u03b1-carbon, `[C@H]` for the urea side-chain carbon, and `[C@H]` for the methoxyethyl carbon on the pyridine. All four correspond to the (S) labels in the drawing.\n\nSMILES: O=C1OCC(C)(C)Cc2c(-c3cccnc3[C@H](C)OC)n(CC)c3ccc(cc23)-c2csc(n2)C[C@H](NC(=O)N(C)C[C@H](C)OC)C(=O)N2CCC[C@@H]1N2"
